+# ClickUp App — FROZEN Design & Contract (orchestrator-owned, immutable)
+
+> Every worker MUST read this file first. The modeling, contract, projection, and tenancy
+> decisions below are FROZEN by the orchestrator. Do NOT re-derive, rename, or "improve" them.
+> You FILL LOGIC into this structure; you NEVER re-make a decomposition decision.
+
+## Bounded contexts (FROZEN)
+
+Two NEW backend bounded contexts under `packages/api/typescript/src/`, plus read-models in `ui`:
+
+1. **`workspace`** — the container hierarchy.
+   - **Workspace** (AggregateRoot): `{ id, name, ownerId }`. Top container. Command: `CreateWorkspace`.
+     Raises `WorkspaceCreatedEvent` (domain).
+   - **Space** (AggregateRoot): `{ id, workspaceId, name, lists: SpaceList[], statuses: TaskStatus[] }`.
+     - `lists` is an ORDERED array of the **SpaceList VALUE OBJECT** `{ listId, name, position }` —
+       NOT its own aggregate. NO List repository / controller / use case / event. Lists are persisted
+       in the `lists` table but loaded/saved ONLY through the Space aggregate (SpaceRepository
+       hydrates `space.lists` from the table).
+     - `statuses` is the space's workflow: an array of `TaskStatus` values. `Space.create` DEFAULTS it
+       to all four `[TODO, IN_PROGRESS, IN_REVIEW, DONE]`.
+     - Commands: `CreateSpace` (creates the space + its initial lists + default statuses),
+       `AddList` (append one SpaceList VO at the next position — the secondary command, DO NOT skip it).
+     - Raises `SpaceCreatedEvent` (domain).
+   - **SpaceRepository** read API (FROZEN — `task` context imports and depends on this):
+     `findById(id: string, tx?): Promise<Space | undefined>` returning a Space whose `.lists`
+     (SpaceList VO[]) and `.statuses` (TaskStatus[]) are populated.
+
+2. **`task`** — the Task aggregate (its OWN context; different lifecycle — moved constantly).
+   - **Task** (AggregateRoot): `{ id, workspaceId, spaceId, listId, title, status: TaskStatus,
+     priority: TaskPriority, assigneeIds: Id[] }`.
+   - INVARIANTS (enforced by the entity, raising NAMED domain errors):
+     - `TASK_STATUS_NOT_IN_SPACE` — a task's `status` must be one of its space's `statuses`.
+     - `LIST_NOT_IN_SPACE` — a task's `listId` must be one of its space's list ids.
+     The use case loads the Space via SpaceRepository and PASSES the allowed statuses + the space's
+     list ids into the entity factory/method; the ENTITY does the membership check and throws.
+     Entity signatures (FROZEN):
+     - `Task.create({ workspaceId, spaceId, listId, title, status, priority, assigneeIds,
+        allowedStatuses: TaskStatus[], spaceListIds: string[] })` → validates listId ∈ spaceListIds
+        (LIST_NOT_IN_SPACE) and status ∈ allowedStatuses (TASK_STATUS_NOT_IN_SPACE).
+     - `task.changeStatus(next: TaskStatus, allowedStatuses: TaskStatus[])` → validates membership,
+        returns the previous status (for the event `fromStatus`).
+     - `task.assign(assigneeIds: string[])` → replaces assignees.
+   - Commands: `CreateTask`, `ChangeStatus`, `AssignTask`. One use case per intent.
+   - Events: `TaskCreatedEvent` (domain), `TaskStatusChangedEvent` (domain — name
+     `task.status_changed`; payload `{ taskId, workspaceId, spaceId, listId, fromStatus, toStatus }`).
+   - **Internal handler** `TaskStatusChangedHandler` (write-side): reacts to the domain
+     `TaskStatusChangedEvent` and PUBLISHES the cross-service **integration** event (see contract)
+     via `ExternalMediator.publish`.
+
+`TaskStatus` and `TaskPriority` are ENUMS, never contexts. Membership/assignees are NOT a separate
+context — assignees are plain user-id strings on the Task; no Member aggregate.
+
+## Tenancy mapping (FROZEN — read carefully)
+
+The template's multi-tenant unit is the tenancy **Store**; the SSE session is scoped by
+`session.storeId`. In THIS app **the Workspace IS the tenant**: `workspaceId === session.storeId`.
+- All `workspace`/`task` use cases derive `workspaceId` / `ownerId` from `ctx.session.storeId`
+  (controllers pass `ctx.session.storeId` as `workspaceId`). One workspace per tenant store.
+- The SSE broadcaster (ui `ListenEvents`) filters task events by `payload.workspaceId === client.storeId`.
+- The frontend reads the active workspaceId from the existing tenancy-scope store (storeId == workspaceId).
+
+## CONTRACT LOCK (FROZEN — author in packages/contracts, then `bun contracts`)
+
+### Enums (TypeSpec) — `packages/contracts/wire/enums/`
+- `task-status.tsp`: `enum TaskStatus { TODO: "TODO", IN_PROGRESS: "IN_PROGRESS", IN_REVIEW: "IN_REVIEW", DONE: "DONE" }`
+- `task-priority.tsp`: `enum TaskPriority { LOW: "LOW", NORMAL: "NORMAL", HIGH: "HIGH", URGENT: "URGENT" }`
+- Add `import "./enums/task-status.tsp";` and `import "./enums/task-priority.tsp";` to `wire/main.tsp`.
+
+### Integration event (TypeSpec) — `packages/contracts/wire/events/task-status-changed.tsp`
+```tsp
+import "./_base.tsp";
+namespace TemplateContracts;
+@doc("Published by the TS task context when a Task moves between statuses. The ui SSE controller relays it to the browser (filtered by workspaceId) to drive the live List/Board views.")
+model TaskStatusChangedEvent extends IntegrationEvent {
+  name: "integration.shared.task.status_changed";
+  @doc("Workspace (== tenant store) the task belongs to — the SSE realtime tenancy filter.")
+  workspaceId: string;
+  taskId: string;
+  fromStatus: TaskStatus;
+  toStatus: TaskStatus;
+}
+```
+- Add `import "./task-status-changed.tsp";` to `wire/events/index.tsp`.
+- Generated TS (verify after `bun contracts`):
+  `@template/contracts-typescript/wire/enums` → `TaskStatus`, `TaskPriority`.
+  `@template/contracts-typescript/wire/events` → `TaskStatusChangedEvent` (class) + `TaskStatusChangedEventSchema`.
+  Construct with `new TaskStatusChangedEvent({ ownerId, payload: { workspaceId, taskId, fromStatus, toStatus } })`.
+
+### Drizzle tables (FROZEN) — new schema files, add exports to `packages/contracts/db/schema/index.ts`
+Mirror the existing tenancy.ts shape (audit cols `created_at/updated_at` tz + `version int default 1`).
+
+`packages/contracts/db/schema/workspace.ts` — `export const workspaceSchema = pgSchema('workspace')`
+- `workspaces`: `id uuid pk defaultRandom`, `name text notNull`, `owner_id uuid notNull`, audit.
+- `spaces`: `id uuid pk`, `workspace_id uuid notNull`, `name text notNull`,
+  `statuses jsonb notNull` (array of TaskStatus strings), audit. index on `workspace_id`.
+- `lists`: `id uuid pk`, `space_id uuid notNull references spaces.id onDelete cascade`,
+  `name text notNull`, `position integer notNull`, audit. index on `space_id`.
+
+`packages/contracts/db/schema/task.ts` — `export const taskSchema = pgSchema('task')`
+- `tasks`: `id uuid pk`, `workspace_id uuid notNull`, `space_id uuid notNull`, `list_id uuid notNull`,
+  `title text notNull`, `status text notNull`, `priority text notNull`,
+  `assignee_ids jsonb notNull default '[]'`, audit. indexes on `space_id`, `list_id`.
+- `task_list_view` (READ MODEL — ListViewProjection): `task_id uuid pk`, `workspace_id uuid notNull`,
+  `space_id uuid notNull`, `list_id uuid notNull`, `title text notNull`, `status text notNull`,
+  `priority text notNull`, `assignee_ids jsonb notNull default '[]'`, audit. index on `(space_id, list_id)`.
+- `task_board_view` (READ MODEL — BoardViewProjection): same columns as `task_list_view`,
+  index on `(space_id, status)`.
+
+Then run (contract-lock worker): `bun contracts` (tsp compile + ts/go codegen + drizzle:generate) and
+`bun migrate:create` if the migration SQL wasn't emitted. Gate: generated enums/event present;
+a new migration `.sql` exists under `db/migrations/`.
+
+### SSE wiring (ui `ListenEvents.ts`) — done by the ui-wire worker, NOT the contract worker
+- Add `{ name: 'integration.shared.task.status_changed' }` to the `BROWSER_EVENTS` array.
+- Change the broadcaster tenancy filter from `storeId` to `workspaceId`:
+  `const tenancy = z.object({ workspaceId: z.uuid() }).loose().safeParse(event.payload)`
+  and match `if (client.storeId === tenancy.data.workspaceId) client.send(event)`.
+- Replace `ListenEventsControllerOutputSchema` with a discriminated union so the SDK emits a typed
+  frontend payload:
+```ts
+export const ListenEventsControllerOutputSchema = z.discriminatedUnion('name', [
+  z.object({
+    name: z.literal('integration.shared.task.status_changed'),
+    ownerId: z.string(),
+    payload: z.object({
+      workspaceId: z.uuid(), taskId: z.uuid(),
+      fromStatus: z.enum(TaskStatus), toStatus: z.enum(TaskStatus),
+    }),
+  }),
+])
+```
+  (import `TaskStatus` from `@template/contracts-typescript/wire/enums`).
+- After all backend controllers exist, run `bun sdk`.
+
+## READ SIDE — two DISTINCT projections (FROZEN)
+
+Both live in `packages/api/typescript/src/ui/projections/`. They are TWO SEPARATE free-record
+projection classes with TWO SEPARATE projector classes and TWO SEPARATE tables — NOT two queries
+over one table. Each projector subscribes to the `task` domain events `TaskCreatedEvent` +
+`TaskStatusChangedEvent` (imported from `@task/events`) and writes ONLY its own table via its repo,
+using the canonical `find → applyEvent → save` flow (insert via `static create(event)` on TaskCreated).
+
+- **ListViewProjection** (`task_list_view`): one row per task. Repo `TaskListViewProjectionRepository`.
+  Projector `ListViewProjector`.
+- **BoardViewProjection** (`task_board_view`): one row per task. Repo `TaskBoardViewProjectionRepository`.
+  Projector `BoardViewProjector`.
+
+BFF queries (ui `usecases/` + `controllers/`):
+- **GetListView** (`GET /list-view?spaceId=`): reads the Space (via SpaceRepository — for list
+  headers incl. EMPTY lists, ordered by position) + `task_list_view` rows; output groups tasks under
+  each list. Output shape: `{ spaceId, lists: [{ listId, name, position, tasks: TaskCardDTO[] }] }`.
+- **GetBoardView** (`GET /board-view?spaceId=`): reads `task_board_view` rows grouped by status into
+  ALL FOUR `TaskStatus` columns (even empty ones — iterate the enum). Output shape:
+  `{ spaceId, columns: [{ status: TaskStatus, tasks: TaskCardDTO[] }] }`.
+- `TaskCardDTO` (shared in both query output schemas):
+  `{ taskId, listId, title, status: z.enum(TaskStatus), priority: z.enum(TaskPriority), assigneeIds: string[] }`.
+- Both controllers use `AuthAccountMiddleware` (+ store-member middleware like other ui queries) and
+  scope by `workspaceId = ctx.session.storeId` AND the `spaceId` query param.
+
+## Frontend (react) — FROZEN shape
+
+Route: `packages/app/react/src/routes/(app)/spaces/$spaceId/index.tsx` (thin shell).
+- `validateSearch` with `z.object({ view: z.enum(['list','board']).default('board') })` — the view is
+  a BOOKMARKABLE search param (NOT useState). `routeApi = getRouteApi('/(app)/spaces/$spaceId/')`.
+- `-components/`:
+  - `SpaceViewSection` (data-owning): reads `view` + `spaceId` via routeApi; renders `BoardViewSection`
+    or `ListViewSection` by a dispatch map on `view` (no if-chain); renders a toggle that updates the
+    `view` search param via `navigate`.
+  - `BoardViewSection`: `useGetBoardView({ spaceId })`, skeleton while pending, renders 4 columns,
+    each column maps tasks to `<TaskCard task={...} />` (leaf, receives task by prop).
+  - `ListViewSection`: `useGetListView({ spaceId })`, renders lists, each maps to `<TaskCard/>`.
+  - EXACTLY ONE realtime subscription: in `SpaceViewSection` (or a small child),
+    `useServerEvents('integration.shared.task.status_changed', e => { if (e.payload.workspaceId !== workspaceId) return; queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: <the active view's query key> }) })`.
+    workspaceId comes from the tenancy-scope store (== storeId).
+  - `TaskCard` (leaf): shows title + status + priority labels (i18n via enums.*), a status-change
+    control (calls `useChangeStatus` mutation) and an assign control (`useAssignTask`). Mutations kept
+    WHOLE — no try/catch, no onError; onSuccess invalidates the view query key.
+  - `CreateTaskDialog`: opened via `useDialogStore().show(<CreateTaskDialog spaceId listId/>)`;
+    TanStack Form validated against `createTaskMutationRequestSchema` from the SDK; calls `useCreateTask`.
+- i18n: add `enums.TaskStatus.{TODO,IN_PROGRESS,IN_REVIEW,DONE}` and
+  `enums.TaskPriority.{LOW,NORMAL,HIGH,URGENT}` to BOTH `locales/pt.json` and `locales/en.json`.
+  Render labels via `t('enums.TaskStatus.' + value)` (typed). NO hardcoded user-facing text; every
+  button label via `t()`. Every actionable button wired (no dead buttons).
+- SDK identifiers become available after `bun sdk`: hooks `useGetListView`, `useGetBoardView`,
+  `useCreateTask`, `useChangeStatus`, `useAssignTask`; schemas `createTaskMutationRequestSchema`,
+  `changeStatusMutationRequestSchema`, `assignTaskMutationRequestSchema`; query keys
+  `getListViewQueryKey`, `getBoardViewQueryKey`; enums `TaskStatusEnum`, `TaskPriorityEnum`; SSE type
+  `ListenEventsQueryResponse`. (Exact names follow Kubb generation from the controller operationIds;
+  inspect the generated SDK if a name differs.)
+
